Presidential elections were held in [[Slovenia]] on 23 October 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Elections: Slovenia President 2022|url=https://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/3814/|access-date=2021-08-29|website=IFES Election Guide}}</ref> Incumbent [[President of Slovenia|President]] [[Borut Pahor]] was ineligible to run for a third consecutive term due to term limits.<ref>{{Cite web |title=President of the Republic of Slovenia |url=https://www.dvk-rs.si/index.php/en/elections/president-of-the-republic-of-slovenia |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220118065153/https://www.dvk-rs.si/index.php/en/elections/president-of-the-republic-of-slovenia |archive-date=18 January 2022 |access-date=2021-08-29 |website=State Election Commission}}</ref> 

As no candidate received a majority of the vote, a [[Two-round system|runoff]] between the top two placing candidates, former foreign minister [[Anže Logar]], an [[Slovenian Democratic Party|SDS]] member running as an independent, and independent former [[Information Commissioner]] [[Nataša Pirc Musar]], took place on 13 November 2022. Pirc Musar won the runoff with 53.86% of the vote, becoming the first female president of Slovenia.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Natasa Pirc-Musar wird erste Präsidentin von Slowenien |language=de |work=Neue Zürcher Zeitung |url=https://www.nzz.ch/international/praesidentschaftswahlen-in-slowenien-natasa-pirc-musar-wird-die-erste-frau-im-hoechsten-amt-ld.1712061?reduced=true |access-date=2022-11-13}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Wahlkommission: Slowenen küren Pirc-Musar zur Präsidentin |url=https://www.zeit.de/zustimmung?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.zeit.de%2Fnews%2F2022-11%2F13%2Fwahlkommission-slowenen-kueren-pirc-musar-zur-praesidentin |access-date=2022-11-13 |website=Zeit}}</ref> 

Logar acknowledged his defeat and congratulated Pirc Musar on her victory.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Wahlkommission: Slowenen küren Pirc-Musar zur Präsidentin |url=https://www.zeit.de/zustimmung?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.zeit.de%2Fnews%2F2022-11%2F13%2Fwahlkommission-slowenen-kueren-pirc-musar-zur-praesidentin |access-date=2022-11-13 |website=Zeit}}</ref>

